window.docContents[123].resolve({"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/The-generated-indexes/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes--The-generated-indexes--Kinds-and-their-algebra":{"contents":"The column that earns this table is Algebra. A kind's authored edges are the complete statement\nof what may be done with it — multiplied by what, divided into what, raised to what power — because\nthe calculus infers none of them. A kind whose Algebra cell is empty supports no arithmetic at all,\nand being able to see that is the point.\n\n* Kind* Identity* Scale* Algebra* Theorems* attenExponent* AVS attenuation exponent* ratio* produced (1)* paramB · vegetationIndex → attenExponentconsumed (1)* transcendental : attenExponent → attenuationK* attenuation_roles_distinct* attenuationK* AVS vegetation attenuation* ratio* produced (1)* transcendental : attenExponent → attenuationKconsumed (3)* jacB · attenuationK → jacB* attenuationK · paramC → paramC* attenuationK · reflectivity → reflectivity* attenuation_roles_distinct* backscatter* AVS backscatter coefficient σ⁰* ratio* produced (2)* paramA · vegetationIndex → backscatter* paramC · reflectivity → backscatter* * jacB* AVS backscatter times NDVI* ratio* produced (2)* jacB · attenuationK → jacB* jacBPartial · reflectivity → jacB* * jacBPartial* AVS NDVI times gain c* ratio* produced (1)* vegetationIndex · paramC → jacBPartialconsumed (1)* jacBPartial · reflectivity → jacB* * paramA* AVS gain a (σ⁰ per NDVI)* ratio* consumed (1)* paramA · vegetationIndex → backscatter* * paramB* AVS rate b (inverse NDVI)* ratio* produced (1)* pureNumber · paramB → paramBconsumed (1)* paramB · vegetationIndex → attenExponent* * paramC* AVS gain c (σ⁰ per reflectivity)* ratio* produced (1)* attenuationK · paramC → paramCconsumed (2)* paramC · reflectivity → backscatter* vegetationIndex · paramC → jacBPartial* * pureNumber* AVS pure number* ratio* consumed (2)* pureNumber · paramB → paramB* pureNumber · vegetationIndex → vegetationIndex* attenuation_roles_distinct* reflectivity* AVS surface reflectivity* ratio* produced (1)* attenuationK · reflectivity → reflectivityconsumed (2)* paramC · reflectivity → backscatter* jacBPartial · reflectivity → jacB* * vegetationIndex* AVS vegetation index* ratio* produced (1)* pureNumber · vegetationIndex → vegetationIndexconsumed (3)* paramB · vegetationIndex → attenExponent* paramA · vegetationIndex → backscatter* vegetationIndex · paramC → jacBPartial* * length* length* ratio* produced (1)* speed · time → length* length_is_speed_times_time* speed* speed* ratio* consumed (1)* speed · time → length* length_is_speed_times_time* time* time* ratio* consumed (1)* speed · time → length* length_is_speed_times_time* massFraction* mass fraction* ratio* * * volumeFraction* volume fraction* ratio* produced (1)* volumeFraction ± volumeFraction → volumeFraction* * dl* 1* ratio* produced (2)* dl · dl → dl* transcendental : dl → dl* pk, tk* height* height* ratio* * * length* length* ratio* * * width* width* ratio* * * mass* mass* ratio* * mass_extensive* lengthK* length* ratio* * * massK* mass* ratio* * instAssemblesGridSMassK* length* length* ratio* * hLen* mass* mass* ratio* * hMass* lengthKind* length* ratio* produced (1)* lengthKind ± lengthKind → lengthKind* hLen* displacement* displacement* ratio* produced (2)* displacement ± displacement → displacement* factor · displacement → displacementconsumed (1)* displacement · displacement → displacementSq* doubled_east, hDisp, hScale, hSquare, vector_add_comm* displacementSq* displacement squared* ratio* produced (1)* displacement · displacement → displacementSq* hSquare* factor* scale factor* ratio* consumed (1)* factor · displacement → displacement* hScale* backscatter* backscatter coefficient* ratio* * * conductivityKind* ionic conductivity* ratio* * * gwc* gravimetric water content* ratio* * * ndvi* vegetation index* ratio* * * reflBistatic* reflectivity* ratio* * * reflMonostatic* reflectivity* ratio* * * reflectivity* reflectivity* ratio* * cholRowQ_magnitudes* refractiveIndexKind* refractive index (n)* ratio* * * relPermKind* relative permittivity* ratio* * * relaxTimeKind* dielectric relaxation time* ratio* * * vwc* volumetric water content* ratio* * * bloodGroup* abo-blood-group* nominal* * * length* length* ratio* * * mass* mass* ratio* * * mohsHardness* mohs-hardness* ordinal* * * bloodGroup* abo-blood-group* nominal* * * length* length* ratio* * * mass* mass* ratio* * * height* height* ratio* * * length* length* ratio* * * width* width* ratio* * \n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009The generated indexes","header":"31.10.1. Kinds and their algebra","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/The-generated-indexes/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes--The-generated-indexes--Kinds-and-their-algebra"},"/Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy/SysML-v2___-a-quantity-model-organized-by-value-representation/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy--SysML-v2___-a-quantity-model-organized-by-value-representation--How-PropertyKindCalculus-takes-the-kind-as-root-instead":{"contents":"PropertyKindCalculus inverts the nesting: axis (A) is the root. A kind-of-property is a\nfirst-class value (KindOfProperty), and a quantity is indexed by its kind —\nQuantity (k : KindOfProperty) — so the kind is fixed before, and independently\nof, any choice of how the value is recorded. Dimension is not the organizing\nprinciple but a forgetful functor \nthat certifies coherence without deciding what is allowed (developed in the\nnext section). Two consequences fall out directly: two kinds that share a\ndimension remain distinct types — so the dimension-1 disambiguation is\nexpressible — and an operation across kinds is a type error rather than a silent\nsuccess. Value representation — the axis SysML v2 puts at the root — sits here as an\northogonal index over the kind, never a layer the kind hangs beneath: R20's\nInFrame f var k R adds the frame and the variance above a Quantity k R whose kind\nwas already fixed without reference to either.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Why a calculus, not a taxonomy\u0009SysML v2: a quantity model organized by value representation","header":"3.3.2. How PropertyKindCalculus takes the kind as root instead","id":"/Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy/SysML-v2___-a-quantity-model-organized-by-value-representation/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy--SysML-v2___-a-quantity-model-organized-by-value-representation--How-PropertyKindCalculus-takes-the-kind-as-root-instead"}});